                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Correspondence between her Majesty’s government and
                        Messrs. Laird Brothers; and an appendix, containing the correspondence
                        between officers of her Majesty’s customs and Captain Inglefield, R. N., and
                        Messrs. Laird Brothers, respecting the iron-clad vessels building at
                        Birkenhead.</hi></head>
                <p>The following letters form the entire correspondence which has passed between
                    Messrs. Laird Brothers and her Majesty’s government respecting the iron-clad
                    vessels.</p>
                <p>The production of these letters, with other papers, was moved for in the House of
                    Commons by Mr. Seymour Fitzgerald, M. P., on the 23d of February last, but was
                    refused by her Majesty’s government.</p>
                <p>They are now published with the permission of Messrs. Laird Brothers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>VACHER &amp; SONS, <hi rendition="#italic">Publishers.</hi></signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">29, <hi rendition="#small-caps">Parliament
                            Street</hi>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">March,</hi> 1864</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
